--- body ---
## Context

Follow-up to tracker 1507 (closed 2026-11-10). The sweep after PR 2402 found
three sibling scripts that walk `~/.claude/projects` only and do not say so:
`scripts/trace-stats.py` (the census; `--projects-dir`, 643 lines),
`scripts/trace-friction.py` (`--projects-dir`, 672 lines) and
`scripts/trace-wall-time.py` (`DEFAULT_ROOT`, 458 lines). Their counts read as
covering the harness's sessions while Codex and Pi sessions are left out, the
defect ticket 1507 fixed in the context audit. The author ruled on
2026-11-10: "Fix the trace- script: default to all surfaces, say what they
did."

What exists: `scripts/trace_events.py` has `read_claude`, `read_codex` and
`read_pi`; `scripts/transcript_spool.py` gives each runtime's live root
(`live_roots()`) and the spool; `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py` (tickets 1508
and 1509) has a table of runtimes with one reader per root and a
read / not read / could not look report. `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py`
imports `trace-stats.py` (`iter_trace_files`, pricing, timestamp parsing).

## Scope

- Each of the three scripts reads, by default, every runtime it can measure
  (Claude Code, Codex, Pi and the Pi spool), and its table and JSON name each
  runtime read, each one not read with the reason, and each one it could not
  look at.
- A measure that has no meaning or no data on a runtime (a price table, a
  tool category, a record type that runtime does not write) is reported as
  not measured there, never as zero.
- The three scripts are one change: the same fix in three parallel units.

Out of scope: reading other hosts (ticket 1516 does that for the context
audit only); new metrics; prices for models that have none in the script
today, beyond saying they are not priced.

## Test

On fixture transcripts, per script: a Codex session and a Pi session are
counted under their runtime beside a Claude Code one; an absent corpus for one
runtime is reported as could not look while the others are counted; a measure
the runtime cannot supply is reported as not measured, not as zero.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `trace-stats.py`, `trace-friction.py` and `trace-wall-time.py` each read
  Claude Code, Codex and Pi sessions by default
- [ ] Each one's output names every runtime read, not read and could not look
  at, and marks a measure a runtime cannot supply as not measured
- [ ] `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py` and its tests still pass unchanged in
  behaviour
- [ ] `make check` passes
